# Build context hygiene. The image build only needs the Go module (go.mod/sum)
# and the source under cmd/ and internal/ (which embeds assets/). Everything else
# is dead weight in the build context (it was ~3.8GB without this file, almost all
# of it books/comics under data/ and loose archives in the repo root).
#
# Keep this in sync with .gitignore's runtime-artifact rules, and exclude anything
# the compiler does not read.

# Secrets: must NEVER enter an image build context.
secrets/
secrets.bak/
*.bak/

# Library data: the library, covers, import staging, the catalog DB. Huge and
# irrelevant to the build (the binary creates/reads these at runtime, not build).
data/

# Books / comics / loan tokens, wherever they sit (repo root included).
*.acsm
*.epub
*.pdf
*.der
*.cbz
*.cbr

# VCS, CI, hooks, and tooling config the compiler doesn't read.
.git/
.github/
.githooks/
.golangci.yml
.markdownlint.json

# Docs and the build/deploy plumbing itself.
docs/
README.md
Makefile
docker/

# Build outputs and test artifacts.
bin/
library
*.test

# Stray installers / Node litter / OS files.
*.dmg
*.pkg
node_modules/
package.json
package-lock.json
.DS_Store
